# HookView needs an Upstash-REST-compatible Redis. Pick ONE of the setups below.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1) Local Docker / Colima (default for `docker compose up` and local `npm run dev`)
#    A `serverless-redis-http` (SRH) container speaks the Upstash REST protocol
#    on top of a plain Redis container. The token is an arbitrary shared secret.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=http://localhost:8079
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=hookview_dev_token

# Inside docker-compose the app reaches SRH by service name instead:
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=http://srh:80

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2) Vercel / production — a real Upstash Redis database
#    Create one at https://console.upstash.com and copy its REST URL + token.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=AX...your-real-token...
